        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "1ffe73b3-c8fd-59a4-a111-78290d601db5",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Byron Edmund Walker\n- Companies: Canadian Bank of Commerce\n- Organizations: University of Toronto, National Gallery of Canada, Champlain Society, Appleby College, Art Gallery of Ontario, Royal Ontario Museum\n- Places: Toronto, Ontario, Canada, Queen's Park\n- Topics: Canadian banking, arts patronage, cultural and educational institutions\n\nFacts:\n- The University of Toronto became a secular institution and assumed its present name in 1850 after originally being controlled by the Church of England.\n- Byron Edmund Walker was a Canadian banker who was born on 14 October 1848 and died on 27 March 1924.\n- The University of Toronto is a public research university in Toronto, Ontario, Canada, on the grounds surrounding Queen's Park.\n- Byron Edmund Walker served as president of the Canadian Bank of Commerce from 1907 to 1924.\n- Byron Edmund Walker was a generous patron of the arts who helped found and nurture the University of Toronto, the National Gallery of Canada, the Champlain Society, Appleby College, the Art Gallery of Ontario, and the Royal Ontario Museum.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "989aa0de-49d5-5aa2-9072-e73429fee905",
        "text": "Page: Byron Edmund Walker. Sentence: Sir Byron Edmund Walker, CVO (14 October 1848 – 27 March 1924) was a Canadian banker.\nPage: Byron Edmund Walker. Sentence: He was the president of the Canadian Bank of Commerce from 1907 to 1924, and a generous patron of the arts, helping to found and nurture many of Canada's cultural and educational institutions, including the University of Toronto, National Gallery of Canada, the Champlain Society, Appleby College, Art Gallery of Ontario and Royal Ontario Museum.\nPage: University of Toronto. Sentence: The University of Toronto (U of T, UToronto, or Toronto) is a public research university in Toronto, Ontario, Canada on the grounds that surround Queen's Park.\nPage: University of Toronto. Sentence: Originally controlled by the Church of England, the university assumed the present name in 1850 upon becoming a secular institution.",
        "type": "DocumentChunk"
      },
